A||||4||billfredmike24||Gonna get speakers installed at shop unless......||||1||
Z||000000||billfredmike24||06-05-2000||04:58 PM||||I've got pioneer 4x10's to go in the dash, is there clips that will plug directly into the cars speaker harness or will i have to splice those wires to install.  If there are clips could someone give me the model number, how much, and where i could buy them.<BR>Also, if someone could give me step by step instructions on how to install without the clips, that would be greatly appreciated.<BR>I've already searched and found nothing.<BR>TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula||06-05-2000||06:48 PM||||Its been a while but I think that there were clips on them and it was pretty much plug and play  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>to install.......(quick version)<P>Left speaker...<BR>pop out the grey top thing with a screw driver.  pop each side to avoid breaking the clips.<P>unscrew (maybe unbolt) the factory speakers.<P>lift the factory speaker and remove the connectors (clips)<BR>(remember wich side goes where (left - left, and right - right)<P>plug the connectors (clips) onto the little silver tabs on the back of your new speaker.<P>screw (bolt) in the new speaker<P>pop the top back on.<P>right speaker.....<BR>pop out the grey top thing with a screw driver.  pop each side to avoid breaking the clips.<P>unscrew (maybe unbolt) the factory speakers.<P>lift the factory speaker and remove the connectors (clips)<BR>(remember wich side goes where (left - left, and right - right)<P>plug the connectors (clips) onto the little silver tabs on the back of your new speaker.<P>screw (bolt) in the new speaker<P>pop the top back on.<P>if confused...... (they are very similiar)<BR>pop out the grey top thing with a screw driver.  pop each side to avoid breaking the clips.<P>unscrew (maybe unbolt) the factory speakers.<P>lift the factory speaker and remove the connectors (clips)<BR>(remember wich side goes where (left - left, and right - right)<P>plug the connectors (clips) onto the little silver tabs on the back of your new speaker.<P>screw (bolt) in the new speaker<P>pop the top back on.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||LarryB||06-05-2000||07:43 PM||||Crutchfield's provides an adapter if you buy the speakers from them, you might be able to buy a pair of adapters from them.  It's easier than having to splice the speakers in.  <BR>The stock harness (at least in the '86) is a flat 2-pronged connector, the Pioneer 4x10s have the 2 small different-sized blade connectors.  You can't directly plug one into the other. <p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 06-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||06-05-2000||10:34 PM||||I changed mine to Pioneers too - a very simple installation regardless of whether you clip or splice -- but -- you need a 7mm socket to remove the four screws holding each speaker............||||reg||1
Z||000004||ROB MAC||06-06-2000||12:16 AM||||When I did mine I found the new speakers made the grills rattle ,presumably because they were bassier and moving more air. So I removed the grills and carefully cut out most of the inner plastic grill leaving enough to support the cloth covering and man if they didnt sound 100% better. Plastic grills can take alot of the highs away.||||reg||1
